include: "<stddef.h>"
include: "mixa_manager/mixa_backend.h"

# Header unit for the clean L2 port of mixa_backend_table (share-and-
# backends ticket 20260913-192700, module 5 of 6). mixa_backend.h is
# real, plain, hand-written C (like mixa_pump.h/mixa_selection.h
# before it) -- no L1 .h.lm1 counterpart exists anywhere in this
# codebase for it (its own top comment records exactly why: converting
# it is planned future work, "H2", blocked on run_mixa.ps1's own .h.
# lm1 -> .lm1.h conversion step not yet being written). Nothing to
# predef here, only the real header itself, reached the exact same
# zero-cost `include:`-not-`predef:` way the real mixa_backend_table.
# lm1/mixa_pump.lm1/every headless-backend-driven module this whole
# session already reaches it. MixaBackend's own field (vt) is
# dereferenced via `\` in the real body with no L1-level struct:
# declaration for MixaBackend/MixaBackendVTable anywhere, proven safe
# by the established finding from ticket 20260913-151000 (mixa_app_
# controller): l1trans's own `\` dereference operator emits a plain C
# `->` and defers ALL structural resolution to gcc. Total distinct
# predef'd files: 0.
